ard extension that it is clear that \"secondary\" has not been implemented in any way for horizontal sharding.  The effort here would involve a major rewrite of how the ManyToManyDP works such that as it generates lists of identifiers to update and delete, it also needs to pass along a list of objects and it then needs to break the work amongst multiple connection objects (which would in the non-shard case be all the same Connection object) in the same way persistence._connections_for_states is used (it should probably use that function).     This is basic functionality that has essentially been missing for at least ten years and this is the first time anyone has pointed it out.\n\nAs for your specific case, since you are able to deal with the BookAuthor object directly, you just need to add viewonly=True to each of your \"secondary\" relationships, which is a good idea in any case if you are working with an explicit association object, and that will prevent the ManyToManyDP from being involved at all.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943395/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://